# CareConnect: rules for Cline (and any other coding agent)

Before ANY task, read in this order and follow them exactly:
1. CLAUDE.md            (stack, structure, styling, security, definition of done; applies to every agent)
2. docs/PLAN.md         (current build plan, decisions, approved components, progress tracker)
3. docs/WORKLOG.md      (where the build is right now)
4. docs/COMPONENTS.md   (existing components: reuse or extend, never copy)

Hard rules:
- Work on ONE phase of docs/PLAN.md per task, on branch feature/multi-doctor. Stop at the end and report.
- Only use existing components or ones marked ✅ in docs/PLAN.md §6. Any other NEW component file: stop and ask Leroy.
- No new dependencies. No hex colours, no backdrop-filter, no raw styled <button>: use the primitives.
- No invented placeholders (contacts, copy, images): ask Leroy.
- Never write or log secrets (admin password, CRON_SECRET, service-role key).
- Never change a decision in docs/PLAN.md §3; add the question to §8 and ask.
- Never apply migrations to the live Supabase project yourself.

Live data (added 2026-11-08 after test scripts changed real accounts):
- There is ONE Supabase project and it is live (the Vercel review site uses it). Treat it as production.
- NEVER change any user's password, email or auth data (no auth.admin.updateUserById / deleteUser in scripts).
- NEVER delete or update rows with the service-role key from a script, and NEVER touch audit_log
  (it is append-only; the database refuses changes).
- Don't write scripts that read SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY from .env.local. Test through the app in the browser.
- To test as a role, ask Leroy to sign in, or ask him for dedicated test accounts. Don't create your own.
- If a check needs data that doesn't exist, STOP and ask instead of seeding or cleaning the live database.

When a phase is done:
- Tick its boxes in docs/PLAN.md (§2 and §7), update docs/WORKLOG.md, COMPONENTS.md, /styleguide, SPEC.md, src/lib/releases.ts as relevant.
- Run: npm run typecheck && npm run lint && npm run build (all must pass).
- Commit, then list every file you created or changed.
